      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LOCHINVAR JAG (1) has been racing well and again did a good job last time when runner-up at this circuit and distance, beaten 1.1 metres after leading. That gave him two wins and two placings from the last four starts. Has the speed to take advantage of the ace draw. JIMMY JAMES MAGUIRE NZ (2) was a beaten favourite last start but had a tough barrier and raced wide so it may pay to be forgiving. Had recorded two wins and a close third from his previous three starts here so is worth another chance aided by the good draw. WITHDISTINCTION (7) went close the last time he raced here two back and owns a good record at this circuit and distance. Draws for a trail and looks dangerous if he gets the gaps. JILLIBY FABIO (8) races well here and was a city winner two back.",
